1: # Signed commutator plumbing for the fixed-edge flop
2: 
3: Working orientation calculation for independent audit, 17 November 2026.
4: The explicit charts below determine a sign which is left adjustable in
5: the last paragraph of Krylov's Theorem2. This note is not yet promoted
6: to a numbered statement.
7: 
8: Use H with ordered real basis (1,i,j,k), and its boundary orientation
9: on the unit S3. Write
10: 
11:     A(s,t)=(t s t^-1,t), B(s,t)=(s,s t s^-1), C=[A,B].
12: 
13: For a boundary map f, let Sigma_f be D4_s times S3_t glued to
14: S3_s times D4_t by the identification right=f(left), with the
15: orientations inherited from the standard boundary of D4_s times D4_t.
16: Here A extends the left piece and B extends the right piece. Thus
17: left composition by a B power and right composition by an A power
18: do not change the oriented diffeomorphism type of Sigma_f.
19: 
20: Take three products D_i=D4_s times D4_t with signs +,-,+. Glue
21: the S3_s times D4_t face of D_1 to that of D_2 by
22: 
23:     s2=s1, t2=s1 t1 s1^-1,
24: 
25: and the D4_s times S3_t face of D_2 to that of D_3 by
26: 
27:     s3=t2^-1 s2 t2, t3=t2.
28: 
29: These maps reverse the induced oriented boundaries because the
30: adjacent eight-ball signs differ. Round the common corners. The two
31: unattached outer faces are the standard oriented left face
32: D4_s times S3_t of D_1 and right face S3_s times D4_t of D_3.
33: Following a point across the intermediate corner gives the boundary
34: word g=A^-1 B. Composing on the right by the extending A and on the
35: left by the extending B^-1 gives
36: 
37:     B^-1 g A = B^-1 A^-1 B A.
38: 
39: In the mapping class group the commutator C is central, so the last
40: word is C^-1. Hence the oriented boundary of this plumbing is
41: Sigma_(C^-1).
42: 
43: There are two zero-section four-spheres. Orient the first by ds on
44: its D_1 hemisphere and -ds on its D_2 hemisphere. Orient the second
45: by dt on its D_2 hemisphere and -dt on its D_3 hemisphere. At their
46: single intersection in D_2, their concatenated tangent orientation
47: is -ds dt, exactly the orientation of D_2. Their intersection is +1.
48: Each normal clutch fixes a real line, so each self-intersection is
49: zero. The exact intersection matrix is therefore
50: 
51:     Q=[[0,1],[1,0]], signature(Q)=0.
52: 
53: On the first sphere the normal transition from its first hemisphere
54: to its second is Ad_s. On the second it is Ad_t^-1. The normal
55: orientations on the two hemispheres of the first sphere are both dt;
56: those on the second sphere are both -ds. Thus the two Pontryagin
57: numbers have opposite signs and absolute value four. Their product
58: is -16, independently of the convention for the sign of the SU2
59: clutch generator. Tangent TS4 has p1=0, so these are also the two
60: evaluations of p1(TW).
61: 
62: The handle description has no homology in degrees1,2,3 and a free
63: rank-two group in degree4. In particular W is spin. Since Q is
64: unimodular, its relative Pontryagin square is
65: 
66:     (p,-p) Q^-1 (p,-p)^t = -32, |p|=4.
67: 
68: The spin Eells--Kuiper formula gives
69: 
70:     mu(Sigma_(C^-1))=(-32-4*0)/896=-1/28,
71:     mu(Sigma_C)=+1/28.
72: 
73: The last equality uses the central disc-supported sphere subgroup
74: and the extension-by-identity identification with the double, with
75: the orientations just specified. The remaining comparison to the
76: complex six-sphere is explicit as follows. In the Cox products
77: u=a0+j a1, v=c0+j conjugate(c1), q=uv, h=u i u^-1,
78: h reverses the complex CP1 orientation and q preserves the original
79: complex normal orientation when H has the ordered basis above.
80: The complex orientation on the exterior D3_h times S3_q is therefore
81: the product orientation. It is the negative of the boundary
82: orientation of D3_h times D4_q on that face. The doubled exterior
83: S3_h times S3_q has the product orientation, so the central
84: disc-supported class C has the same positive Eells--Kuiper sign in
85: the complex exterior marking.
86: 
87: Together with the independently audited coefficient n=-6A in
88: notes/part3_flop_relative_group.md, this computation fixes the proposed
89: fixed-edge correction as +n in the positive Theta_7 generator. The
90: actual chart/product and boundary-word comparisons above are retained
91: for independent audit before any new return value is exported.
